{"type":"after","callId":"call@184","endTime":48441.714,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/Command reference\n    \n\nCommand reference\nEvery command we know of — host → tagger, tagger → host, headset — with args, meaning and confidence\n✅bench🔍app👥communityLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nHow to read the tables.\"Direction\" is host→gun () or gun→host (). Provenance is per row: ✅bench we sent/received it on hardware and know what it did; 🔍app the command class and its field names come from the Callsign app's IL2CPP metadata (names certain, wire position = declaration order); 👥community seen in LaserTagMods sources or community captures, not reproduced by us. Commands the app knows but we have never sent sit in their own table at the end of this page. Where a command's field map has its own page (, /, ) the row links there.Source: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (confidence note), protocol/brx-protocol.md §3–§4\nHost → tagger: lifecycle & configuration21 rows\n\n\nCommand\nDir\nArgs\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nConnectivity check. Reply .\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nStop. First frame the official app sends on every (re)connect; also part of the end-of-game tail.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nApp-controlled mode: opens the live event tap (buttons, ), locks the on-gun menu. Reply .\n✅bench\n\n\n / \n>>\n—\nOn the known-safe list. Sent on v4.32: no observable reply.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nClear current game state. First frame of every arm sequence; half of the panic sequence.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nBegin the configuration sequence. Gun echoes .\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n8 tokens\nGlobal game settings — friendly fire, indoor/outdoor, region, ambient light, gyro, BT secondaries, crit modifier, mods. No respawn/time/lives token. → GSET page\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nid, 0, HP, armor, shield, 50, , voice-pack…\nPlayer settings: token 1 = player id (0–63), tokens 3–5 = HP/armor/shield pools, then a positional voice pack. → PSET page\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nslot 0–5 + ~43 tokens\nDefine a weapon in a slot: damage, fire interval, fire mode, clip/reserve, reload, sounds, IR type. → WEAP page\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n8 tokens\nIncoming-IR effects matrix: what an IR word with protocol B / subtype U does to this gun. Unmatched cells are silently ignored. → SIR page\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nbutton id, function, 4 swap slots\nRemap physical controls. Buttons: 0 trigger · 1 alt-fire · 2 reload handle · 3 select · 4 left · 5 right · 8 gyro. Functions seen: 0 fire · 97 reload · 98 (select/left/right) · 100 weapon-cycle · 4 melee (gyro). Mandatory — without it the trigger only chirps \"disabled\".\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nteam\nTeam id. Masked to 2 bits () → four native teams 0–3. Drives the gun LED colour at  (1 = blue, 2 = yellow observed) and is echoed as  token 4 on the victim. A live write changes hit resolution immediately but does not repaint LEDs.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\none empty token\nGo-live and respawn. Restores HP/armor and (on respawn) ammo; echoes . Also clears the  fn-23 state ( token 2 back to 100).  (no empty token) is not the same command.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nslot, magazine, reserve, 1\nLoad magazines. Must follow  at initial go-live or the gun is live with no ammunition. e.g. . A bare  re-push resets ammo to the frame's baked values — re-send  after any weapon swap.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n0\nStop/clear sound playback. Sent right after  on connect and just before the go-live cue.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n8 tokens\nPlay a sound id (see the 2166-id bank). Two independent slots: token 1 = local/effect sound, token 4 = announcer/voice channel —  speaks \"kill\" with token 1 empty;  uses both. Tokens 2–3 are required:  is silent,  speaks. Numeric values vary by client ( Android app ·  iOS ·  JEDGE). APK field names: soundName, addToQue1, addToQue2, loopingTime, stun, isNeedQueue.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nvolume, 0\nMaster volume. Android app sends ; iOS . 30 is inaudible for game audio; use 69.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nname\nSets the gun's persistent name (the USB  field; survives power-cycle). Opening the official app rewrites it to .\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nQuery firmware. Reply  — token 2 is the headset firmware () when a headset is linked.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nn\nEnd-of-game / stop.  is the second half of the panic sequence. Do not probe it mid-game hoping for a score — the gun keeps none.\n👥community\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nOver BLE returns a -framed status array () plus a . Not the USB device record (that is USB-only — see the Serial console page).\n✅bench\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §3, §7a, §7e, §7f, §7l, §7o, §7r; docs/gotchas.md; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24 $QUERY)\nHost → tagger: in-game effects, feedback & pools12 rows\n\n\nCommand\nDir\nArgs\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nThe shooter's green-sight kill-confirm flash. The host sends exactly one per kill the holder scores, ~0.4 s after the trigger burst ends. (The APK lists it under notifications; on the wire the phone sends it.)\n✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\naddedHP, addedArmor, addedShields\nGrant health. Additive, clamped at the pool max — not an absolute set. Writes do not self-emit ; the new value shows on the next hit/HUD refresh.\n🔍app ✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\nhP, armor, shields\nAdjust current pools. Same additive/clamped behaviour as .\n🔍app ✅bench\n\n\n\n>>\ndamage, isCriticalShot, powerLevel\nFour shapes sent on v4.32: each was echoed and applied no damage.\n🔍app (fields) ✅bench (bench result)\n\n\n\n>>\nRange, CountIRPulses, RateOfFire, FlashLED\nFive shapes sent on v4.32: zero IR emitted (receiver control passing before and after).\n🔍app (fields) ✅bench (bench result)\n\n\n\n>>\niRPower, soundOnHit, rangeOutdoor, rangeIndoor\nFive shapes sent on v4.32: zero IR emitted (receiver control passing before and after).\n🔍app (fields) ✅bench (bench result)\n\n\n\n>>\nintensity\n returns  and fires no IR.\n🔍app ✅bench(no-op)\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nListed in the APK. Proven no-op over BLE.\n🔍app ✅bench(no-op)\n\n\n\n>>\nmid, effect, optionA, optionB\nGun LED effect —  = LedEffect enum (Solid, Glow, ChaseBack, ChaseForward, StopIR). Not RGB: colour is team-derived from . Used by the app during the pre-game lobby.\n🔍app ✅bench(not RGB)\n\n\n\n>>\niRType, crit, modifier, indoorMode, operationMode, channel, GrenadeType, MaxCount\nSmart Grenade configuration frame, addressed to the gun. GrenadeMode enum: FlashBang / Gas / Confusion / Molotov. Sent on the bench: the gun emitted IR, but the emitted bits did not track the arguments.\n🔍app (fields) ✅bench (bench result)\n\n\n\n>>\nenum index\nThe \"playbook\" pre-battle family mirroring the on-gun menu — a second remote-start path captured on fw v4.30 ( = FFA ·  = M4 AUTO ·  = Body Armor ·  = 5 lives ·  = infinite).  produced a \"game starting\" reload sound on our v4.32.\n👥community\n\n\n\nhost↔host\n—\nJEDGE's device-to-device kill notification. A host-side convention, not a tagger command.\n👥community\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §3, §7d, §7i, §7j(community $PB*), §7o; protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-26 headset emission, $BHIT, $GREN emission)\nHeadset commands (host → gun → headset)2 rows\n\n\nCommand\nArgs (APK)\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n\nLedColorType (White, Pink, Orange; + green via ), BlinkLoopType (Once, ThreeTimes, Infinite), LedEffectType (incl. Heartbeat)\nHeadset LED. Exactly this frame is sent in the app's end-of-game tail and in the lobby.\n✅bench(captured) 🔍app(fields)\n\n\n\na, b\nSent by the app ~1.7 s after every death.\n✅bench(captured) 🔍app(fields)\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §3, §7e, §7f; protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (Enums)\nTagger → host: events and echoes11 rows\n\n\nMessage\nFields\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n\n—\nReply to .\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nVersion reply; token 2 reads  with a headset linked,  otherwise.  = developer/host image.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n—\nGun-initiated disconnect notice (e.g. the moment its headset is switched off).\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nBattery telemetry, ~every 30 s in app mode. Token 1 = pack millivolts (7.662 V), token 2 = cell millivolts (3.921 V). Tokens 3–4: — (unknown).\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nHealth/armor HUD echo.  → all zeros;  → pools + current weapon's ammo; death → . Tokens 3–4: — (unknown). A zeroed  after  means \"no config loaded\" (post power-cycle tell).\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nAmmo/weapon HUD stream. Per-round during fire and reload (mag 0→1→2… as reserve drains). Token 2: — (unknown) — reads 100 in normal play and drops to 0 after a  fn 23 hit. Token 3 = weapon slot. Token 5 = weapon heat (0–100+, only on overheat weapons). Only streams on ammo events — silence is not \"no change\".\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nHit received. → Events page for the full decode.\n✅bench\n\n\n\ne.g. \nPools after a hit; arrives in the same millisecond as its .  = death.\n✅bench\n\n\n\nid 0–5, state 1 press / 0 release\nPhysical button event (ids match ). Streams only in app mode.  is also returned by .\n✅bench\n\n\n\n~11  pairs\nStatus array in reply to BLE .\n✅bench\n\n\n /  / \n—\nSelection echoes from the on-gun menus (LaserTagMods).\n👥community\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §4, §7e, §7f, §7j, §7r; mcp/brx_mcp/protocol.py (parsers); docs/experiment-log.md 2026-08-27\nSeen in the app's vocabulary, not exercised by usfacts about the Callsign app's request namespace only; on-tagger behaviour has not been observed. 🔍app7 rows\n\n\nCommand\nDirection\nAPK fields / enums\nNote\n\n\n\n\n>>\n\nNever sent by us.\n\n\n\n>>\n—\nNever sent by us.\n\n\n\n>>\n~38 event→sound slots: ActionKey, DeathAlarm, TickTock, HitHp, HitArmor, HitShield, HitCrit, EmpStart/Loop/End, IncendiaryStart/…, TearGasHit, …\nNever sent by us.\n\n\n\n>>\n (+ SetVolume)\nNever sent by us.\n\n\n /  → \n>> / <<\n\nThe app's premium-content (BattleCoins) handshake. The metadata names three premium modes: Generals, Commanders, Swarm. Never sent by us.\n\n\n ·  · \n>> (headset)\n—\nListed with the headset commands. Never sent by us.\n\n\n\n<<\n—\nListed as a notification. Never observed on the wire.\n\n\nSource: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md\nComplete vocabulary from the app's own request namespace(🔍app): AMMO ASKDLC ASSIST BHIT BMAP BUMP CLEAR DLC FSET GLED GREN GSET HFIRE IRTX LIFE MELEE NAME PLAY PLAYX PSET SIR SPAWN START STOP STUN VERSION VIB VOL WEAP ZOOM · headset BLINK CHASE HLED HLOOP LED · notifications ALCD BUT GOTDLC HIR HP LCD SFLASH TIME VERSION VOLTS. , , , and the  family are not in it — they come from LaserTagMods and our bench. Absence from the app ≠ non-existent.Source: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@184"}
